fn make()! { return mut [0]; }
say f = make;
say bad = [f()];
// An opaque call hides its return capability, so the checker admits the element and defers to a
// runtime seal-check that traps the mutable value landing in the immutable container.
// error(full):
// error: cannot store a mutable value in an immutable container
//  --> mutable_in_immutable_runtime.say:3:12
//   |
// 2 | say f = make;
// 3 | say bad = [f()];
//   |            ^^^^ this container is immutable
//   |
//   = help: an element is mutable; freeze it, or mark the container `mut`
